---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SEOHead from '../components/SEOHead.astro';
import { url } from '../utils/paths';
---
<Base title="Fractional CMO and AI marketing services" description="Four ways to work with Manual Focus. Strategic Advisor, Fractional CMO, Build & Hand Over, and Manual Focus AI, where we run the AI workflows for you.">
  <SEOHead slot="seo" type="service" title="Fractional CMO and AI marketing services" description="Four ways to work with Manual Focus. Strategic Advisor, Fractional CMO, Build & Hand Over, and Manual Focus AI, where we run the AI workflows for you." breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Services', url: '/services/' }]} />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">SERVICES</div>
      <h1>How we work together</h1>
      <p class="lead">Three ways to work with us, each building AI into the workflows your team already runs. And one product, Manual Focus AI, where we run the workflows and deliver the output. Every engagement starts with a free 30-minute working session.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Strategic Advisor -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-detail reveal">
        <div class="service-tag mono">/01 · STRATEGIC ADVISOR</div>
        <h2>Your team ships. Nobody's steering.</h2>
        <p class="service-for">For companies with a marketing team but no senior leader running it.</p>
        <p>You have people doing the work. What you don't have is someone senior calling the shots, reviewing the output and asking the harder questions. We sit alongside the team for a handful of sessions a month, giving you the strategic input of a CMO without the cost or commitment of one.</p>

        <h3>What this looks like</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Weekly or fortnightly working sessions on what to do next</li>
          <li>Reviews of campaigns, content and creative before they ship</li>
          <li>Quarterly planning and priority-setting with the team</li>
          <li>Briefings on the AI tooling and emerging tech worth using, and where it fits the workflows your team already runs</li>
          <li>Hiring and team-shape advice as you grow the function</li>
          <li>Direct line between sessions for the calls that won't wait</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What this is not</h3>
        <p>We won't run your team for you, ship the work on your behalf, or sit in every meeting. This is senior input on a part-time cadence, not embedded leadership.</p>

        <p class="service-shape mono">Shape · 1–2 days a month. Day rate or monthly retainer.</p>
        <p class="service-proof">James currently advises AI-powered wealth managers in this shape.</p>
        <a href={`${url('/enquire/')}?offer=strategic-advisor`} class="btn-cta" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">Book a free working session</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Fractional CMO -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-detail reveal">
        <div class="service-tag mono">/02 · FRACTIONAL CMO</div>
        <h2>You need a CMO. Not a full-time one.</h2>
        <p class="service-for">For companies that need senior marketing leadership without a full-time hire.</p>
        <p>We embed in your leadership team. We set the marketing thesis, build the plan, lead the people you already have, and ship the pieces that need senior hands. AI and emerging tech are wired into the workflows your team already runs, so a small team moves like a much larger one. You get the seniority of a CMO at a fraction of the cost, with execution shipped alongside the strategy.</p>

        <h3>What this looks like</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Marketing thesis, 90-day plan and quarterly OKRs</li>
          <li>Leading and growing the existing team (or hiring it)</li>
          <li>Embedding AI and emerging tech into the workflows your team already runs, day by day</li>
          <li>Shipping key campaigns, launches and content with that leverage in place</li>
          <li>Owning reporting to the CEO and board</li>
          <li>Inputs into product, pricing and positioning decisions</li>
          <li>Bringing the Forge tooling to compress production cycles</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What this is not</h3>
        <p>A deck without the work to deliver it. You get a senior marketer who ships as well as plans. It isn't unlimited time either. The seat is part-time by design, so the cadence is set up to make the most of it.</p>

        <p class="service-shape mono">Shape · 1–2 days a week. Three-month minimum.</p>
        <p class="service-proof">James has led marketing from the inside at RGT Cycling, which he co-founded and grew from 19k to 350k users before Wahoo acquired it, and for a $200M privacy-focused digital asset.</p>
        <a href={`${url('/enquire/')}?offer=fractional-cmo`} class="btn-cta" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">Book a free working session</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Build & Hand Over -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-detail reveal">
        <div class="service-tag mono">/03 · BUILD &amp; HAND OVER</div>
        <h2>You know what you need. It isn't built yet.</h2>
        <p class="service-for">For companies that know what they need built, and want it shipped fast.</p>
        <p>You have a specific marketing outcome in mind, whether that's a launch, a website rebuild, an SEO programme, a brand refresh or a content engine. We build it end-to-end with AI and emerging tech wired into the build (not bolted on after), then hand it back to your team to operate, with documentation and training to keep it running.</p>

        <h3>What this looks like</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Product or feature launches, with positioning, narrative and assets</li>
          <li>Commerce rebuilds on Shopify, BigCommerce or WooCommerce/WordPress, full-stack or headless, shipped fast</li>
          <li>Headless web architectures: composable stacks built for speed, SEO and a clean handover</li>
          <li>Landing systems and conversion infrastructure (Next, Astro, Webflow where it fits)</li>
          <li>SEO and answer-engine optimisation programmes, including content engines</li>
          <li>Brand refreshes with messaging architecture and visual direction</li>
          <li>PR campaigns with journalist outreach, story arcs and placement</li>
          <li>AI and emerging-tech workflows embedded into your existing stack, not a parallel one</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What this is not</h3>
        <p>It's not a retainer dressed up as a project. The scope is fixed up front, the price is fixed up front, and the handover is real. After it's shipped, your team owns it.</p>

        <p class="service-shape mono">Shape · Fixed scope, fixed timeline, fixed price. Typical builds 4–12 weeks.</p>
        <p class="service-proof">See the method on our own site: the <a href={url('/lens/ops/site-audit-and-refresh/')}>September 2026 audit and refresh</a>, with the retest logs published.</p>
        <a href={`${url('/enquire/')}?offer=build-and-hand-over`} class="btn-cta" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">Book a free working session</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- /04 Manual Focus AI · the product -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-detail service-detail-product reveal">
        <div class="service-tag mono">/04 · MANUAL FOCUS · AI <span class="service-tag-flag">PRODUCT</span></div>
        <h2>We run the AI workflows. You get the output.</h2>
        <p class="service-for">For CTOs, CMOs and existing teams who can't carve out the time to stay current with new models, build pipelines or learn another tool every week.</p>
        <p>Manual Focus AI is the product side of the agency. Instead of teaching your team to run the workflows, we own them. Content planning, wireframing and production sit inside Manual Focus, run on the Forge, and the output lands in your stack on an agreed cadence. When a new model ships that's better than the one we were using, we swap it in. You don't see any of that, you just keep getting better output.</p>

        <h3>What this looks like</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Content planning pipelines: calendars, briefs, drafts, fact-checks</li>
          <li>Wireframing and creative production: landing pages, ad units, social packs</li>
          <li>Research and synthesis: competitor moves, SERP shifts, model launches, distilled weekly</li>
          <li>Pipelines maintained and re-tooled as new models and capabilities ship</li>
          <li>Output delivered in your brand and your stack, ready to use, not just ready to edit</li>
          <li>No internal training, no tool sprawl, no learning curve for your team</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What this is not</h3>
        <p>There's nobody to manage and no tool to learn. Manual Focus owns and runs the workflows, tuned to your brand and priorities, and the output arrives on cadence.</p>

        <p class="service-shape mono">Shape · Monthly retainer. Output on agreed cadence. Three-month minimum.</p>
        <p class="service-proof">See it running: the <a href={url('/lens/content/news-desk/')}>news desk</a> behind our own AI briefing shortlists the day's stories and publishes only the ones that clear the bar.</p>
        <a href={`${url('/enquire/')}?offer=manual-focus-ai`} class="btn-cta" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">Book a free working session</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Specialism note -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">VERTICAL DEPTH</div>
      <h2 class="vertical-headline">Endurance and sports brands<br/>are where we've shipped the most.</h2>
      <p class="vertical-copy">If you're building in endurance, sports or the broader fitness category, you're getting a team that has run marketing in your category at scale. Our founder, James Vickers, co-founded RGT Cycling and took it from 19k to 350k users before Wahoo Fitness acquired it. Beyond that, we've led marketing across AI, fintech, hardware and digital assets, so the playbook travels. For the search side, read the <a href={url('/blog/seo-playbook-premium-endurance-brands/')}>SEO playbook for premium endurance brands</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">WHAT HAPPENS NEXT</div>
      <ol class="next-steps-list">
        <li><strong>A free 30-minute working session.</strong> You bring the problem, we bring questions and a first view on it.</li>
        <li><strong>A written scope, if it's a fit.</strong> The shape of the engagement and the cost. Builds get a fixed price up front.</li>
        <li><strong>We start.</strong> Fractional CMO engagements set the thesis and a 90-day plan inside the first month.</li>
      </ol>
      <a href={url('/enquire/')} class="btn-cta" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">Book a free working session</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: 760px;
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  .service-detail {
    max-width: var(--max-width);
  }

  /* Product tier — distinct from the three engagement tiers above */
  .service-detail-product {
    position: relative;
    padding: var(--space-md);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: 4px;
    background:
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(192, 38, 211, 0.05), rgba(0, 229, 255, 0.02)),
      var(--color-bg);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .service-detail-product::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
    height: 3px;
    background: var(--color-cta-gradient);
  }
  .service-tag-flag {
    margin-left: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.55rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-cta-end);
    color: var(--color-cta-end);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 0.625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    background: rgba(0, 229, 255, 0.06);
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .service-detail-product { padding: var(--space-lg); }
  }

  .service-tag {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .service-for {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-style: italic;
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .service-detail > p {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .service-detail h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .service-detail ul {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    padding-left: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .service-detail ul li {
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .service-proof {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .service-proof a,
  .vertical-copy a { color: var(--color-text); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }

  .next-steps-list {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 760px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .next-steps-list strong { color: var(--color-text); }

  .service-shape {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    padding-top: var(--space-sm);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .vertical-headline {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1;
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .vertical-copy {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 760px;
  }
</style>
